  "Overall Assessment": "Both initiatives are excellent, addressing the same profound problem with a highly innovative and citizen-centric solution. They are nearly identical, sharing core strengths in Impact and Innovation (the highest-weighted criteria). The decisive difference is that Project B demonstrates a marginally higher degree of innovation and a more comprehensive evidence-gathering approach by including an additional, thoughtful test ('gradual disclosure') aimed at optimizing user engagement. This slight edge in iterative design and learning capability makes it the preferable investment, assuming the same level of risk and resource requirement as Project A."
